<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Backing Connected App for the GTM_Employee_SSO Auth Provider (issue #106).

  Purpose: let an internal rep who is already authenticated on the org's own
  lightning.force.com domain SSO into the GTM1 Experience Cloud site without
  retyping credentials, via the standard "Login with Salesforce" mechanism
  (a same-org Auth Provider backed by this Connected App). See
  TASK_SCOPE.md §3 for the rejected alternatives and why this is the
  supported, auditable path.

  Deliberately no <profileName>/<permissionSetName> entries: omitting both
  is what keeps this Connected App's "Permitted Users" setting at "All users
  may self-authorize" rather than "Admin approved users are pre-authorized",
  so no permission-set grant is required for a rep to use it (internal users
  only — a guest/prospect never holds an internal session to bridge in the
  first place, so this exposes nothing to them). If a later hardening pass
  switches to admin-approved users, GTM_Offering_User and GTM_Offering_Admin
  would each need this app added to their assigned-app list — see
  TASK_SCOPE.md §3 item 5.

  <consumerKey> is intentionally absent: Salesforce generates the Consumer
  Key/Secret pair on first deploy of a new Connected App. Manual step 1 in
  TASK_SCOPE.md retrieves that generated Consumer Key/Secret from Setup and
  pastes them into authproviders/GTM_Employee_SSO.authprovider-meta.xml —
  they are never set here.

  callbackUrl is the SITE's own domain and path prefix
  (https://<site-domain>/<sitePathPrefix>/services/authcallback/GTM_Employee_SSO),
  NOT the org's my.salesforce.com domain, confirmed live against gtm-dev
  (issue #106): the OAuth authorize request Salesforce generates for an
  Auth Provider triggered from a site's login page always targets that
  site's own domain, and a mismatched callback here fails with
  redirect_uri_mismatch. An earlier version of this file used the org
  domain and failed live for exactly that reason.
-->
<ConnectedApp xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <label>GTM Employee SSO</label>
    <contactEmail>REPLACE_WITH_ORG_ADMIN_EMAIL@example.com</contactEmail>
    <description>Backs the &quot;Login with Salesforce&quot; Auth Provider that lets an internal rep SSO from the org into the GTM1 Experience Cloud site. See TASK_SCOPE.md for issue #106.</description>
    <oauthConfig>
        <callbackUrl>https://REPLACE_WITH_SITE_DOMAIN/REPLACE_WITH_SITE_PATH_PREFIX/services/authcallback/GTM_Employee_SSO</callbackUrl>
        <isAdminApproved>false</isAdminApproved>
        <isConsumerSecretOptional>false</isConsumerSecretOptional>
        <scopes>Api</scopes>
        <scopes>Web</scopes>
        <scopes>RefreshToken</scopes>
    </oauthConfig>
    <oauthPolicy>
        <ipRelaxation>ENFORCE</ipRelaxation>
        <refreshTokenPolicy>infinite</refreshTokenPolicy>
    </oauthPolicy>
</ConnectedApp>
